%S A401226 1,4,15,58,227,864,3190,11502,40549,140863,482755,1636860,5497794,
%T A401226 18325769,60680951,199805730,654689084,2136126987,6943882121,
%U A401226 22498556584,72683969470,234200648829,752857989563,2414947785198,7731276494484,24706497081903,78821609212829
%N A401226 Number of largest sets S of points of the 3 X n grid as in A401223, counted up to the reflections of the grid in its horizontal and vertical axes and the half turn.
%C A401226 For n = 3 only these four symmetries of the rectangle are used. Under all eight symmetries of the 3 X 3 square there are 10 classes.
%C A401226 By Burnside's lemma, a(n) = (A401223(n) + r(n) + v(n) + w(n))/4, where r(n), v(n), w(n) count the sets fixed by the reflection in the middle row, the reversal of the columns and the half turn. For n >= 4, r(n) = 0, and for even n >= 4 also v(n) = 0 and w(n) = 2*n*3^(n/2-2).
%C A401226 The analogous count for the 2 X n grid is A322284(n-1) for n >= 2.
%C A401226 The g.f. comes from transfer matrices for the sets fixed by each symmetry (see the Pemmasani link). Listing the fixed sets directly agrees for n <= 24, and listing all the sets and their orbits agrees for n <= 10.
%H A401226 Arjun Pemmasani, <a href="/A401226/b401226.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A401226 Peter Kagey, <a href="https://peterkagey.com/problems/001/">Open Problem Collection, Problem 001</a>.
%H A401226 Arjun Pemmasani, <a href="https://github.com/apemm/Kagey-Problems/blob/main/kagey-problems/problem001/jis/pemmasani.pdf">Maximum Blackouts That Keep Every Lattice Rectangle Identifiable</a>, preprint, 2026.
%H A401226 Arjun Pemmasani, <a href="https://github.com/apemm/Kagey-Problems/tree/main/kagey-problems/problem001">Solvers, exhaustive verification, and pre-registration ledger for Problem 001</a> (GitHub repository).
%F A401226 G.f.: x*(1 - 11*x + 40*x^2 - 24*x^3 - 177*x^4 + 383*x^5 - 257*x^6 + 163*x^7 + 809*x^8 - 2202*x^9 - 2918*x^10 + 2958*x^11 + 12261*x^12 - 3496*x^13 + 4315*x^14 - 24275*x^15 - 39018*x^16 + 30876*x^17 + 38988*x^18 - 9604*x^19 + 32060*x^20 - 11536*x^21 - 30904*x^22 + 100264*x^23 + 41200*x^24 - 85584*x^25 - 116448*x^26 - 151200*x^27 - 112896*x^28 - 29376*x^29)/((1-3*x)^3*(1+2*x^2)^3*(1-3*x^2)^2*(1+2*x^4)*(1-2*x-2*x^2)^3*(1-2*x^2-2*x^4)).
%F A401226 a(n) = (A401223(n) + 2*n*3^(n/2-2))/4 for even n >= 4.
%o A401226 (PARI) my(x='x+O('x^30)); Vec(x*(1 - 11*x + 40*x^2 - 24*x^3 - 177*x^4 + 383*x^5 - 257*x^6 + 163*x^7 + 809*x^8 - 2202*x^9 - 2918*x^10 + 2958*x^11 + 12261*x^12 - 3496*x^13 + 4315*x^14 - 24275*x^15 - 39018*x^16 + 30876*x^17 + 38988*x^18 - 9604*x^19 + 32060*x^20 - 11536*x^21 - 30904*x^22 + 100264*x^23 + 41200*x^24 - 85584*x^25 - 116448*x^26 - 151200*x^27 - 112896*x^28 - 29376*x^29)/((1-3*x)^3*(1+2*x^2)^3*(1-3*x^2)^2*(1+2*x^4)*(1-2*x-2*x^2)^3*(1-2*x^2-2*x^4)))
